WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:06.464
Down by the tree of life lives.

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:08.800
A haunting flock of pure blankness.

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:12.512
I'm coming to check on our lesser
flamingos.

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:15.640
These guys are from Africa.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.599
Hi, guys.

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:19.310
Good morning.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:21.980
How are you doing?

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.982
Hi, everybody.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:27.068
It's egg laying season
for the lesser flamingos.

00:00:27.485 --> 00:00:30.405
And the potential parents are busy.

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:32.574
But it hasn't always been this way.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:37.954
We've had absolutely no luck breeding
these birds.

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:40.540
We have had one chick in 20 years.

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:43.835
We always have a plan, but

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:46.546
in nature, our plan
doesn't always fit in with the reality.

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:50.633
So sometimes that we can have
what we feel is a fantastic season.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:53.470
Lots of rain, lots of nest building,
but no eggs.

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:57.348
It's a bad time for no breeding.

00:00:57.348 --> 00:01:01.186
All species of flamingos are under
some type of environmental pressure.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.439
Out of all the species, lessers

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:07.567
are probably the one that are
the most threatened at this time.

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:11.279
They're feeling a lot of pressure
in the world in regards

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:15.116
to habitat loss and habitat destruction.

00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:20.622
To encourage more romance between looks
for ways to improve the habitat itself.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.042
The team decided
they wanted to try something different

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.127
with the nesting material.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:29.672
It was an email

00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:33.301
that I received from Animal Kingdom
and it was a big surprise.

00:01:33.676 --> 00:01:34.260
Disney's Animal

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.764
Kingdom asked if they could borrow
some baseball play for their flamingos.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:42.185
It's a special combination of clay
and sand

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:46.815
that really works well with this Florida
climate, with the rain and the humidity.

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:50.860
It's really malleable when it's wet,
but it hardens really strongly

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:54.114
when it's dry
and the birds just really took to it.

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:57.575
Containing more clay than Florida soil.

00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:01.496
The infield mix passed the flamingo
nest test

00:02:02.705 --> 00:02:05.834
and egg appeared,
and then they were on a roll.

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:10.046
I don't know what's in this clay,
but we're going to call it Magic Clay

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.215
because we're already at egg five or six.

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:13.174
They're really excited.

00:02:13.174 --> 00:02:16.845
We thought we had our plan together
and the flamingos are on the same page.

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:20.098
But only one egg proved fertile.

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:23.893
And for the parents of that egg disaster
struck.

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:29.023
The father suffered from a leg injury,
so we had to take him up to our hospital.

00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:32.485
There are processes,
the paper lays the egg and then

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:35.280
one incubates while the other one eats,
and then they sweat.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.782
But the mom couldn't raise the egg
by herself.

00:02:38.032 --> 00:02:42.954
Flamingos are serially monogamous,
so with the biological parents down,

00:02:43.246 --> 00:02:47.709
the team looks for another solution
that can be found in nature in the wild.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.712
It's not uncommon
for same sex pairs to bond.

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:54.591
They build these strong relationships
that can last for years.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:59.012
We decided that our best option
was actually to give the egg

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:05.185
to our really great pair of male birds.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:09.606
Same sex pair
blush and bashful swoop in to the rescue.

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:12.609
These two boys have been together
for a long time.

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:14.652
They've never shown any interest in

00:03:14.652 --> 00:03:17.655
any of the females
that have come over to Discovery Island.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.659
We don't want to give the egg
to the other pairs

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:24.662
because that would stop them
from possibly producing their own.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:29.834
These potential dads quickly make a
connection with their new responsibility.

00:03:30.835 --> 00:03:33.046
The blushing, bashful got the egg

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.882
and the whole time
they were talking to the egg,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:39.177
which is very important,
it connects them to the chick.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.430
So they were making that connection
and building that bond.

00:03:42.972 --> 00:03:47.310
The boys tucked the only fertilized egg
safely under their caring wings.

00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:50.438
The future of the flock now rests on them.

00:03:50.772 --> 00:03:53.483
We're hoping that instinct will kick in
and they'll know exactly what

00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:55.568
to do.

